      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using the Scalar Multiplication Property",
      "problem": "If $\\,T\\,$ is a linear transformation and $\\,T([\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}]$, then find $T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]).$\n\n| $\\,T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}])=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, it must satisfy $T(kv)=kT(v).$ Noting that $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]=2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T([\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]) & =T(2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}])=2T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since we're told that \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
