    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-317722",
      "knowledge_point_id": "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication",
      "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(-6{v}_{1}+5{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-kv+hw)=T(-kv)+T(hw)=-kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-6{v}_{1}+5{v}_{2}) & =-6T({v}_{1})+5T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}] & =-6T({v}_{1})+5[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =5[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -39\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 6T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2"
            },
