    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-317817",
      "knowledge_point_id": "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Image of a Vector Under a Map Using Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication",
      "problem": "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$, then find $T({v}_{1}).$\n\n| $T({v}_{1})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+w)=T(kv)+T(w)=kT(v)+T(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}] & =3T({v}_{1})+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
